From 0998b81df2d7004d15601054bc8e9f50c19df0b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nassos Yiannopoulos <nassosyian@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:33:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 51/54] hw/display/pvg/pvg-exec: limit attachment
 upload/write-back to the damage rectangle of a pass
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Union of scissor ∩ viewport over a segment's draws; attachments with load
action Load or DontCare only transfer that rectangle (~250 MiB saved per 500
command buffers on the desktop). Property damage-limit (default on).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 hw/display/pvg-linux-pci.c |   6 +-
 hw/display/pvg/pvg-exec.c  | 152 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 hw/display/pvg/pvg-exec.h  |   5 +-
 hw/display/trace-events    |   2 +-
